course: dictionary
lesson: 7598
title: Primrose: a flower, a colour, a name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «A primrose has five pale yellow petals with a darker centre that guides insects to the nectar» is about a flower, because it has petals and nectar.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like petals and insects show a plant. Words like yellow show a colour. A character called Primrose in a story shows a name. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: The name has an old story behind it. Primroses flower very early in spring, so they are like the first rose of the year. The name comes from the Latin «prima rosa», which means the first rose.
explain: The phrase «the primrose path» is different again. It is an old saying for an easy, pleasant way that leads to trouble, so the words around it tell you it is not really about a flower at all.
fact: A primrose is a small wild plant with pale yellow flowers.
fact: Primroses bloom early in spring and grow in woods, hedges and banks, in Britain and Europe.
fact: Primrose is also a soft, pale yellow colour, called primrose yellow.
fact: The name comes from the Latin «prima rosa», meaning the first rose, because it flowers so early.
fact: Primrose can be a girl's name, and «the primrose path» means an easy, pleasant way that leads to trouble.
exercise: «A primrose has five pale yellow petals with a darker centre that guides insects to the nectar.» What is a primrose in this sentence? | A kind of spring weather | *A small wild plant with pale yellow flowers | An easy path that leads to trouble | A girl called Primrose
exercise: The name comes from old words meaning «first rose». Why is the primrose called that? | It is always the biggest flower in the wood | It grows only on the tops of hills | *It flowers very early, like the first rose of spring | It smells exactly like a rose
exercise: Lily says, «The primrose path looks lovely, so let's walk it.» In the phrase «the primrose path», what does primrose mean? | A path lined with yellow flowers | A path up a steep hill | A quick way home | *An easy, pleasant way that may lead to trouble
test: Which colour is primrose yellow? | *A soft, pale yellow | Dark green | Deep blue | Bright red
test: Where would you usually find primroses growing? | On the open sea | *In woods, hedges and on banks | In a desert | Inside a shop
exam: Mia says primrose can only mean a flower. Is Mia right? | Yes, because the colour is a different word | *No, it can also mean a colour, a girl's name, or a saying like «the primrose path» | Yes, it can only ever mean a flower
